{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "traer-backend-collection-clean-v2",
    "name": "Traer Backend API",
    "description": "Postman collection synced with source code (cmd/api/main.go + internal/handlers/*.go).\n\nLIVE ROUTES (10): GET / | POST /login | POST /users | POST /logout | POST /jobs/create (auth) | GET /jobs (auth) | PUT /users?id= (auth) | DELETE /users?id= (auth) | GET /users/id?id= (auth) | GET /users/email?email= (auth).\n\nDISABLED (commented out in cmd/api/main.go:103-106, handlers commented in internal/handlers/job.go:113,119,153,169): GET /jobs/status | POST /jobs/retry | GET /jobs/download | GET /instances/get — kept in place with [DISABLED in code] suffix and will return 404 until uncommented.\n\nAuth: backend issues HttpOnly `token` cookie on POST /login (24h expiry). AuthMiddleware (internal/handlers/auth.go) reads `token` cookie, validates JWT, injects user_id+email into context. Authenticated requests must send that cookie (Postman cookie jar auto-persists it). POST /logout clears the cookie (requires cookie to exist, else 401).\n\nOrder: Register User -> Login -> [authenticated] Create Job -> List All Jobs -> User operations.\n\nKNOWN CODE BUG (internal/handlers/job.go:50-52): HandleCreateJobs decodes {urls, process_type} into req but then builds `var urls []string` and ranges over the empty local instead of req.URLs, so it ALWAYS returns 400 \"url is required\" until fixed (change to `for _, u := range req.URLs`). Collection body below shows the intended schema.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Base URL of the Traer API; do not add a trailing slash."
    },
    {
      "key": "jobId",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Job ID for the disabled endpoints (GET /jobs/status, POST /jobs/retry, GET /jobs/download use ?id=). No live endpoint returns a job ID yet."
    },
    {
      "key": "userId",
      "value": "1",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "User ID used by user update/delete/lookup requests (must be numeric; backend parses with strconv.Atoi)."
    },
    {
      "key": "userEmail",
      "value": "test@example.com",
      "type": "string",
      "description": "Email used by register/login/lookup requests."
    }
  ],
